# What `gcloud builds submit` uploads to Cloud Build.
#
# WITHOUT THIS FILE gcloud generates one from .gitignore -- which works by
# accident here (data/ is gitignored) but is fragile: the day someone
# un-ignores a data path, every build starts uploading gigabytes over the
# network. Be explicit instead.
#
# NOTE: this is NOT the same as .dockerignore. This controls what leaves your
# machine; .dockerignore controls what the Docker build can COPY. Both are
# needed, and they should stay roughly in sync.

.git/
.gitignore

# 17 GB. The container reads the dataset from a GCS bucket mount at runtime.
data/

# Local virtualenvs -- multi-GB and useless on a Linux builder.
save-the-knees-env/
.venv/
venv/

notebooks/
Docs/
david_not_public/
api/

# The React front end. 471 MB of node_modules, and the serving image COPYs
# only functions/, serving/ and models/ -- none of this has ever been in the
# container. Without this line every build ships half a gigabyte.
Frontend/

**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

requirements-dev.txt
*.md

# Never upload local credentials to a build. See also .gitignore.
.env
*.json.key
*-key.json
service-account*.json
